## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design high-frequency data handling in React: memoized selectors, minimal re-renders, and virtualization for performance, plus real-world concerns like bursts and cleanup.

## Key Concepts
- Memoized selectors (segment+second buckets)
- React.memo for render-stable Heatmap
- Virtualization (react-window) for large segment sets
- useTransition for burst updates

## Code Example
```javascript
// selector (pseudo)
const bucketSelector = createSelector(
  (s) => s.events,
  (events) => {
    const map = new Map();
    for (const e of events) {
      const sec = Math.floor(e.ts / 1000);
      const key = `${e.segment}|${sec}`;
      map.set(key, (map.get(key) ?? 0) + 1);
    }
    // convert to 2D array by segment
    const result = [];
    // ... populate per-segment buckets
    return result;
  }
);

// Heatmap component
const Heatmap = React.memo(function Heatmap({ data }) {
  // render cells based on data[segment][time]
  return <div>Heatmap grid</div>
});
```

